{"Success":true,"Data":{"State":"open","OpenTime":0,"CloseTime":0,"IsApproved":true,"IsPinned":false,"IsDeleted":false,"IsHidden":false,"IsArchived":false,"IsFollowing":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanReply":true,"CanFollow":true,"TotalPosts":13,"QueuedPosts":0,"DeletedPosts":0,"HasUnreadPosts":true,"HasAttachments":false,"Views":694,"MovedTo":null,"MovedOn":0,"FirstPostId":1884749,"Rating":0,"RatingHits":0,"Starter":{"Id":281938,"Name":"DestoWeddingers","Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"IsOnline":false},"StartDate":1422623125,"LastPoster":{"Id":281816,"Name":"maybeoneday","Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"IsOnline":true},"PollState":"0","LastVote":0,"ForumId":14,"Preview":{"Id":1884749,"PostDate":1422623125,"PostContent":"Hello \u00a0 We are a Canadian couple looking to get married in Mexico \/ Cuba \/ Dominican. \u00a0I am looki...","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"steve.preddy@gmail.com","IpAddress":"184.71.129.214","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1422541795,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"DestoWeddingers","Id":281938,"Name":"DestoWeddingers","IsOnline":false}},"Posts":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"184.71.129.214","IsFirstPost":true,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78709,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"d38fde90af68b48acaf0a769ac532cbc","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Hello&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We are a Canadian couple looking to get married in Mexico \/ Cuba \/ Dominican. &amp;nbsp;I am looking over some of the Mexican Laws, and they quote stressful and confusing. &amp;nbsp;Does anyone have any advise on these?? What tests we need?? What documents?? Do we have to get married before or after in Canada so that the \"ceremony\" in Mexico is real?? Also, we have been bounced around by FA&#039;s since we started trying to plan. &amp;nbsp;Does anyone have any contacts of a good TA in the BC lower mainland??&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:24px;\"&gt;HELP!!&amp;nbsp; :(&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:24px;\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n\n\tMarriage in Mexico: An Introduction\n&lt;p style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;Mexico has some excellent places to get married alongside some picture perfect scenarios. From golden beaches with turquoise waters, to old colonial cities with their charm, old buildings, cobbled streets domes and archways.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;Mexico is becoming increasingly popular as a destination for American and Canadians to get married, and given the opportunity to get married amongst stunning scenery, it&#039;s not hard to see why!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;If you want to get married in Mexico, there is nothing legal or technical stopping you from doing so; but you will need to plan ahead and get a few documents together, fill in a few forms and pay a few fees. This guide will steer you through the maze.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;If after having read through this guide you wonder if you can face the paperwork and admin, don&#039;t panic!&amp;nbsp; You can hire&amp;nbsp;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.mexperience.com\/mexico-weddings\/getting-married-in-mexico.php#PlanWed&#039;&gt;Wedding Planners&lt;\/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;to take care of the detail and paperwork on your behalf in return for a modest fee.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;[&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.mexperience.com\/mexico-weddings\/getting-married-in-mexico.php#TOP&#039;&gt;Menu&lt;\/a&gt;]&lt;\/p&gt;\n\n\t&lt;a&gt;&lt;\/a&gt;Legal Requirements for a Marriage in Mexico\n\n\tConsent\n&lt;p style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;People under the age of 18 may not get married in Mexico without parental consent.   With parental consent, boys have to be at least 16 and girls need to be at least 14 years of age.&lt;\/p&gt;\n\n\tForeigners Getting Married to Foreigners\n&lt;p style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;You don&#039;t need to be resident in Mexico in order to get married here, you&#039;ll just need a passport and your tourist permit, plus some other paperwork (see below). If you plan to get married to a Mexican in Mexico, you will need additional documentation - read the section just ahead...&lt;\/p&gt;\n\n\tChest X-rays and Blood Tests\n&lt;p style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;These must be done locally in Mexico, as the results of the blood tests and the X-ray documentation must be in Spanish and the tests need to be done within a certain time frame of the Marriage Application Form being completed.   Not all Mexican States require the Chest X-rays: Check locally or ask your&amp;nbsp;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.mexperience.com\/mexico-weddings\/getting-married-in-mexico.php#PlanWed&#039;&gt;wedding planner&lt;\/a&gt;.&lt;\/p&gt;\n\n\tFour Witnesses\n&lt;p style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;You will need to have 4 witnesses present at the legal ceremony, and they must have valid identification: usually a valid Passport is used, but other forms of government-issued identification are valid too.&lt;\/p&gt;\n\n\tValidity Outside of Mexico\n&lt;p style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;Your Marriage Certificate will be valid world-wide, BUT you should get your certificate &#039;legalized&#039; in Mexico to ensure it is legally accepted when you get back home. The process is the reverse of getting your native documentation legalized by the necessary authorities (e.g. Foreign Office \/ State Department) for marriage in Mexico (see below); The registry office in Mexico will tell you where this can be done locally or if you hire a&amp;nbsp;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.mexperience.com\/mexico-weddings\/getting-married-in-mexico.php#PlanWed&#039;&gt;wedding planner&lt;\/a&gt;, he\/she will advise.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;[&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.mexperience.com\/mexico-weddings\/getting-married-in-mexico.php#TOP&#039;&gt;Menu&lt;\/a&gt;]&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1884749,"PostDate":1422623125,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Hello<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We are a Canadian couple looking to get married in Mexico \/ Cuba \/ Dominican. \u00a0I am looking over some of the Mexican Laws, and they quote stressful and confusing. \u00a0Does anyone have any advise on these?? What tests we need?? What documents?? Do we have to get married before or after in Canada so that the \"ceremony\" in Mexico is real?? Also, we have been bounced around by FA's since we started trying to plan. \u00a0Does anyone have any contacts of a good TA in the BC lower mainland??\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-size:24px\">HELP!!\u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/sad.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':(' \/><\/span><span  style=\"font-size:24px\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n\n\tMarriage in Mexico: An Introduction\n<p  style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">Mexico has some excellent places to get married alongside some picture perfect scenarios. From golden beaches with turquoise waters, to old colonial cities with their charm, old buildings, cobbled streets domes and archways.<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">Mexico is becoming increasingly popular as a destination for American and Canadians to get married, and given the opportunity to get married amongst stunning scenery, it's not hard to see why!<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">If you want to get married in Mexico, there is nothing legal or technical stopping you from doing so; but you will need to plan ahead and get a few documents together, fill in a few forms and pay a few fees. This guide will steer you through the maze.<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">If after having read through this guide you wonder if you can face the paperwork and admin, don't panic!\u00a0 You can hire\u00a0<a href='http:\/\/www.mexperience.com\/mexico-weddings\/getting-married-in-mexico.php#PlanWed' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>Wedding Planners<\/a>\u00a0to take care of the detail and paperwork on your behalf in return for a modest fee.<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">[<a href='http:\/\/www.mexperience.com\/mexico-weddings\/getting-married-in-mexico.php#TOP' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>Menu<\/a>]<\/p>\n\n\t<a><\/a>Legal Requirements for a Marriage in Mexico\n\n\tConsent\n<p  style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">People under the age of 18 may not get married in Mexico without parental consent.\u00a0\u00a0 With parental consent, boys have to be at least 16 and girls need to be at least 14 years of age.<\/p>\n\n\tForeigners Getting Married to Foreigners\n<p  style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">You don't need to be resident in Mexico in order to get married here, you'll just need a passport and your tourist permit, plus some other paperwork (see below). If you plan to get married to a Mexican in Mexico, you will need additional documentation - read the section just ahead...<\/p>\n\n\tChest X-rays and Blood Tests\n<p  style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">These must be done locally in Mexico, as the results of the blood tests and the X-ray documentation must be in Spanish and the tests need to be done within a certain time frame of the Marriage Application Form being completed.\u00a0\u00a0 Not all Mexican States require the Chest X-rays: Check locally or ask your\u00a0<a href='http:\/\/www.mexperience.com\/mexico-weddings\/getting-married-in-mexico.php#PlanWed' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>wedding planner<\/a>.<\/p>\n\n\tFour Witnesses\n<p  style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">You will need to have 4 witnesses present at the legal ceremony, and they must have valid identification: usually a valid Passport is used, but other forms of government-issued identification are valid too.<\/p>\n\n\tValidity Outside of Mexico\n<p  style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">Your Marriage Certificate will be valid world-wide, BUT you should get your certificate 'legalized' in Mexico to ensure it is legally accepted when you get back home. The process is the reverse of getting your native documentation legalized by the necessary authorities (e.g. Foreign Office \/ State Department) for marriage in Mexico (see below); The registry office in Mexico will tell you where this can be done locally or if you hire a\u00a0<a href='http:\/\/www.mexperience.com\/mexico-weddings\/getting-married-in-mexico.php#PlanWed' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>wedding planner<\/a>, he\/she will advise.<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-size:9pt;color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">[<a href='http:\/\/www.mexperience.com\/mexico-weddings\/getting-married-in-mexico.php#TOP' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>Menu<\/a>]<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"steve.preddy@gmail.com","IpAddress":"184.71.129.214","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1422541795,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"DestoWeddingers","Id":281938,"Name":"DestoWeddingers","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"143.58.161.6","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78709,"EditedBy":"<strong>Edited by JenniferH114, 30 January 2015 - 01:17 PM.<\/strong>","EditDate":1422623822,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":4,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"e0b11ce3e9b14ce43737b5a430f1409e","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@&lt;span&gt;&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281938-destoweddingers\/&#039; title=\"\"&gt;&lt;span&gt;DestoWeddingers&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;- First, let me say that a symbolic vs. a legal ceremony is really a matter of personal preference. That aside, I can only speak to what I know about Mexico, which is where we are getting married. Most people&amp;nbsp;choose a symbolic ceremony and get legally married at home either before or after their trip. Getting legally married in Mexico requires the things you listed above. It is rather costly because documents have to be legally translated and sometimes apostilled. There can also be a lengthy waiting period before you receive your legal documents. I have read many times that even the wedding coordinators at the resorts do not recommend a legal ceremony. Again, this is all a matter of preference. Some people are fine with the process.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We are doing a symbolic ceremony and getting married at the courthouse the weekend before our wedding. We will use our Mexican wedding date as our anniversary date. :)&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1884750,"PostDate":1422623797,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<span><a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281938-destoweddingers\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><span>DestoWeddingers<\/span><\/a><\/span>\u00a0- First, let me say that a symbolic vs. a legal ceremony is really a matter of personal preference. That aside, I can only speak to what I know about Mexico, which is where we are getting married. Most people\u00a0choose a symbolic ceremony and get legally married at home either before or after their trip. Getting legally married in Mexico requires the things you listed above. It is rather costly because documents have to be legally translated and sometimes apostilled. There can also be a lengthy waiting period before you receive your legal documents. I have read many times that even the wedding coordinators at the resorts do not recommend a legal ceremony. Again, this is all a matter of preference. Some people are fine with the process.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We are doing a symbolic ceremony and getting married at the courthouse the weekend before our wedding. We will use our Mexican wedding date as our anniversary date. <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"jhowe114@gmail.com","IpAddress":"38.98.131.98","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1402401189,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-278395.jpg?_r=1421871115","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":285,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"JenniferH114","Id":278395,"Name":"JenniferH114","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"184.56.31.100","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78709,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"cdabcf124151b355d2c07430cb200b66","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;I know legally getting married in Mexico gets a bad rep. I personally did not like the idea of starting our marriage with not being 100% truthful with the people that have traveled so far to celebrate with us and picking which date for an anniversary. My brother did the legal and it was fine, they didn&#039;t have any problems. They actually got the documents translated when they got back home because it was cheaper that way. They did not do a chest xray but they did do a blood test which was quick, harmless and done right on the resort. Check with your resort coordinator to see what is required. At ours we just have to pay for the blood test which is $180. It&#039;s a personal preference that is up to you and your FI!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1884751,"PostDate":1422626135,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>I know legally getting married in Mexico gets a bad rep. I personally did not like the idea of starting our marriage with not being 100% truthful with the people that have traveled so far to celebrate with us and picking which date for an anniversary. My brother did the legal and it was fine, they didn't have any problems. They actually got the documents translated when they got back home because it was cheaper that way. They did not do a chest xray but they did do a blood test which was quick, harmless and done right on the resort. Check with your resort coordinator to see what is required. At ours we just have to pay for the blood test which is $180. It's a personal preference that is up to you and your FI!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"jsparrow@kent.edu","IpAddress":"74.218.117.250","GroupId":47,"GroupName":"Site Supporter","JoinDate":1400492742,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"jsparrow10","Id":278025,"Name":"jsparrow10","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"159.53.46.142","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78709,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"d13b08ec03f36240347ec0a8320f9a2d","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;My sister got married in Mexico and did a legal ceremony and didn&#039;t have any issues. They did have to do the blood test and be in the country 3 days before, but she didn&#039;t find it to be a problem at all. Everything with documentation was completely fine.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1884761,"PostDate":1422634080,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>My sister got married in Mexico and did a legal ceremony and didn't have any issues. They did have to do the blood test and be in the country 3 days before, but she didn't find it to be a problem at all. Everything with documentation was completely fine.<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"rebecca.shaffer@gmail.com","IpAddress":"159.53.174.144","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1403090887,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"beckys98","Id":278581,"Name":"beckys98","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"96.48.159.21","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78709,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"80ac3cf97569be618f17228608af91c4","RawContent":"@[member=\"DestoWeddingers\"] we&#039;ve chosen to do a legal ceremony in Mexico, Riviera Maya to be exact and we just have to get a blood test at the resort, bring a notarized copy of our birth certificates, be at the resort 3 days before the ceremony and have a couple of witnesses over the age of 18. We do have to pay for the apostille and to get docs translated but it was only around $500. \n\n\nI have an amazing destination wedding TA from BC lower mainland so pm me if you want her contact info. She&#039;s wonderful!","Attachments":[],"Id":1884762,"PostDate":1422636503,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281938\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281938-destoweddingers\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">DestoWeddingers<\/span><\/a> we've chosen to do a legal ceremony in Mexico, Riviera Maya to be exact and we just have to get a blood test at the resort, bring a notarized copy of our birth certificates, be at the resort 3 days before the ceremony and have a couple of witnesses over the age of 18. We do have to pay for the apostille and to get docs translated but it was only around $500. <br><br>\nI have an amazing destination wedding TA from BC lower mainland so pm me if you want her contact info. She's wonderful!\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"jerilee.valenzuela@shaw.ca","IpAddress":"24.114.26.77","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1410073385,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-279721.jpg?_r=1420071985","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Wafflesmom","Id":279721,"Name":"Wafflesmom","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"184.151.178.75","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78709,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"f0aab34003e64f9776e2fee01f3eab48","RawContent":"The other ladies are totally right in that it&#039;s very much a personal preference. My husband and I had each been married before so we had extra documentation that was required which was our divorce papers. When I looked into having everything translated and apostilled it was going to be expensive for only that reason. Otherwise we would have done the legal thing in Mexico. Instead we opted for Jamaica because the paperwork requirement was a lot easier.  There are a lot of people that get married in Mexico and never have an issue but of course it&#039;s the ones that might have a problem that you hear about. I was of the same mind and didn&#039;t want two different dates. For me personally I felt it was wrong. My step-son did it and his father and I both had an issue with it. That is only our personal feelings. By all means talk with your resort coordinator and see how much help they will be. Like everything else there are good ones and bad ones and you&#039;ll get a feel for how much they&#039;re going to help you out. If you aren&#039;t totally comfortable with the process you could always consider another country like Jamaica where it&#039;s a bit easier or do like many other brides here and do your legal marriage at home before you go.\n\n\nGood luck!","Attachments":[],"Id":1884763,"PostDate":1422637181,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                The other ladies are totally right in that it's very much a personal preference. My husband and I had each been married before so we had extra documentation that was required which was our divorce papers. When I looked into having everything translated and apostilled it was going to be expensive for only that reason. Otherwise we would have done the legal thing in Mexico. Instead we opted for Jamaica because the paperwork requirement was a lot easier.  There are a lot of people that get married in Mexico and never have an issue but of course it's the ones that might have a problem that you hear about. I was of the same mind and didn't want two different dates. For me personally I felt it was wrong. My step-son did it and his father and I both had an issue with it. That is only our personal feelings. By all means talk with your resort coordinator and see how much help they will be. Like everything else there are good ones and bad ones and you'll get a feel for how much they're going to help you out. If you aren't totally comfortable with the process you could always consider another country like Jamaica where it's a bit easier or do like many other brides here and do your legal marriage at home before you go.<br><br>\nGood luck!\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"achadwick9@yahoo.ca","IpAddress":"206.223.185.220","GroupId":38,"GroupName":"Moderators","JoinDate":1283433799,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-232000.jpg?_r=1426134867","PhotoWidth":668,"PhotoHeight":600,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"acw271011","Id":232000,"Name":"acw271011","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"143.58.161.6","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78709,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"c38c37e7b6ff342518cad3522dffba22","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@&lt;span&gt;&lt;a  class=\"\" href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281938-destoweddingers\/\" title=\"\"&gt;&lt;span&gt;DestoWeddingers&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;- PS: I just saw the chest x-ray part. I haven&#039;t come across that requirement before, but definitely the blood test.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1884951,"PostDate":1422875882,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<span><a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281938-destoweddingers\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><span>DestoWeddingers<\/span><\/a><\/span>\u00a0- PS: I just saw the chest x-ray part. I haven't come across that requirement before, but definitely the blood test.<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"jhowe114@gmail.com","IpAddress":"38.98.131.98","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1402401189,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-278395.jpg?_r=1421871115","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":285,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"JenniferH114","Id":278395,"Name":"JenniferH114","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"187.252.52.125","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78709,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"63b11227d915c40b5c9dfff6ff18c467","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Hey Destoweddingers,&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;in shot this is what you will need, and your hotel coordinator should be able to help, in the riviera maya you only are required to do the blood test.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;div style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);font-size:13.3333339691162px;\"&gt;here are the requirements for a legal ceremony in mexico.&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);font-size:13.3333339691162px;\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);font-size:13.3333339691162px;\"&gt;\n&lt;div style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px;\"&gt;Copy of the passport and tourist card ( its issued at the airport)&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px;\"&gt;Divorce papers if applicable&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px;\"&gt;Blood test for HIV and Health Certificate must be done in mexico within 7 days before the wedding&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px;\"&gt;4&amp;nbsp;witnesses&amp;nbsp;must be over 18 and be present for the ceremony in order to sign the marriage certificate (we need their passport copies)&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px;\"&gt;Completed application form ( we can fill that out for you)&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px;\"&gt;the ceremony can be performed both in english or spanish&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px;\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px;\"&gt;Once Legally married, you will receive a certificate, but the legal act called Acta de Matrimonio, will be send to Chetumal the capital of the State in order to be&amp;nbsp;annotated.&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px;\"&gt;Once we receive the&amp;nbsp;authorized&amp;nbsp;copy we will send it to you via DHL&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px;\"&gt;Usually takes 3 weeks maximum.&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px;\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px;\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:13.3333339691162px;\"&gt;As a couple and your witnesses are obligated to be 4 working days in mexico before the wedding&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px;\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px;\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px;\"&gt;The ceremony takes about 20 minutes maximum. if you need us to get you the 4 witnesses this will have an additional cost.&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;\/div&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1885011,"PostDate":1422903781,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Hey Destoweddingers,<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>in shot this is what you will need, and your hotel coordinator should be able to help, in the riviera maya you only are required to do the blood test.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40)\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<div  style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);font-size:13.3333339691162px\">here are the requirements for a legal ceremony in mexico.<\/div>\n<div  style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);font-size:13.3333339691162px\">\u00a0<\/div>\n<div  style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);font-size:13.3333339691162px\">\n<div  style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Copy of the passport and tourist card ( its issued at the airport)<\/div>\n<div  style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Divorce papers if applicable<\/div>\n<div  style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Blood test for HIV and Health Certificate must be done in mexico within 7 days before the wedding<\/div>\n<div  style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px\">4\u00a0witnesses\u00a0must be over 18 and be present for the ceremony in order to sign the marriage certificate (we need their passport copies)<\/div>\n<div  style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Completed application form ( we can fill that out for you)<\/div>\n<div  style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px\">the ceremony can be performed both in english or spanish<\/div>\n<div  style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px\">\u00a0<\/div>\n<div  style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Once Legally married, you will receive a certificate, but the legal act called Acta de Matrimonio, will be send to Chetumal the capital of the State in order to be\u00a0annotated.<\/div>\n<div  style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Once we receive the\u00a0authorized\u00a0copy we will send it to you via DHL<\/div>\n<div  style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Usually takes 3 weeks maximum.<\/div>\n<div  style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px\">\u00a0<\/div>\n<div  style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px\">\u00a0<\/div>\n<div  style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><span  style=\"font-size:13.3333339691162px\">As a couple and your witnesses are obligated to be 4 working days in mexico before the wedding<\/span><\/div>\n<div  style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px\">\u00a0<\/div>\n<div  style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px\">\u00a0<\/div>\n<div  style=\"margin:0px;font-family:arial, sans-serif;font-size:13px\">The ceremony takes about 20 minutes maximum. if you need us to get you the 4 witnesses this will have an additional cost.<\/div>\n<\/div>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>Dream Weddings Riviera Maya- We pay attention to your wishes and coordinate closely with you to ensure your wedding or event is planned to perfection!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color:rgb(40,40,40);\"><span style=\"font-family:arial;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">Dream Weddings Riviera Maya<\/span><\/span><\/span><br><span style=\"font-family:arial;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">weddingsinplayadelcarmen@gmail.com<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.dreamweddingsrivieramaya.com\/Home_Page.html'>http:\/\/www.dreamweddingsrivieramaya.com\/Home_Page.html<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color:rgb(40,40,40);\"><span style=\"font-family:arial;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">Happy Planning!<\/span><\/span><\/span><br><span style=\"color:rgb(40,40,40);\"><span style=\"font-family:arial;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">Joyce<\/span><\/span><\/span><br>\n\u00a0","Email":"weddingsinplayadelcarmen@gmail.com","IpAddress":"187.252.44.28","GroupId":49,"GroupName":"Insiders","JoinDate":1326829187,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-250090.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"dreamweddings","Id":250090,"Name":"dreamweddings","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"50.137.211.49","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78709,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"b6a6b0318ea23d9a08667ee115b95592","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the tips!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1889281,"PostDate":1426366108,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Thanks for the tips!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"phimoez@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"50.137.211.49","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1425851436,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"MNsunseeker","Id":282367,"Name":"MNsunseeker","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"177.237.111.26","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78709,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"f05f428d85432b394f3d46baa109195d","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the forum, DestoWeddingers, and Congrats on your upcoming destination wedding!!!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We&#039;re a Canadian owned Photo Studio based in Playa del Carmen, so of course are biased to our incomparable Mayan Riviera.&amp;nbsp;It&#039;s is a very popular choice for so many wedding couples, and here are some visual reasons why.....enjoy!!!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;....from a recent &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/media\/set\/?set=a.10153148788044487.1073741924.18683524486&amp;amp;type=3&#039;&gt;Secrets Maroma Wedding Album&lt;\/a&gt;.....&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"https:\/\/scontent-dfw.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xap1\/t31.0-8\/11046670_10153148790769487_1654431620799399918_o.jpg\" alt=\"11046670_10153148790769487_1654431620799\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;...and this one from their &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/media\/set\/?set=a.10153148760879487.1073741923.18683524486&amp;amp;type=3&#039;&gt;Jungle Trash The Dress Photo Session&lt;\/a&gt;......&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"https:\/\/fbcdn-sphotos-e-a.akamaihd.net\/hphotos-ak-xpa1\/t31.0-8\/11032149_10153148762849487_364000385808957458_o.jpg\" alt=\"11032149_10153148762849487_3640003858089\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Wishing you happy research, and all the best with your plans - cheers!!! team MTM :)&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1889312,"PostDate":1426423237,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Welcome to the forum, DestoWeddingers, and Congrats on your upcoming destination wedding!!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We're a Canadian owned Photo Studio based in Playa del Carmen, so of course are biased to our incomparable Mayan Riviera.\u00a0It's is a very popular choice for so many wedding couples, and here are some visual reasons why.....enjoy!!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>....from a recent <a href='https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/media\/set\/?set=a.10153148788044487.1073741924.18683524486&type=3' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>Secrets Maroma Wedding Album<\/a>.....<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"https:\/\/scontent-dfw.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xap1\/t31.0-8\/11046670_10153148790769487_1654431620799399918_o.jpg\" alt=\"11046670_10153148790769487_1654431620799\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>...and this one from their <a href='https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/media\/set\/?set=a.10153148760879487.1073741923.18683524486&type=3' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>Jungle Trash The Dress Photo Session<\/a>......<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"https:\/\/fbcdn-sphotos-e-a.akamaihd.net\/hphotos-ak-xpa1\/t31.0-8\/11032149_10153148762849487_364000385808957458_o.jpg\" alt=\"11032149_10153148762849487_3640003858089\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wishing you happy research, and all the best with your plans - cheers!!! team MTM <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p><img src=\"http:\/\/i711.photobucket.com\/albums\/ww116\/momentsthatmatter\/MTMLogo08-1.png\" alt=\"MTMLogo08-1.png\"><\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.momentsthatmatterphotography.com'><strong><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">Moments That Matter Photography Studios, Playa del Carmen, Mexico<\/span><\/strong><\/a><\/p>\n<p>Canadian Award Winning Photojournalist serving Mayan Riviera<br>\nEmail: <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='mailto:contact@momentsthatmatterphotography.com'>contact@momentsthatmatterphotography.com<\/a><\/p>\n<p>Scoop on what we do:\u00a0 <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/reviews\/r\/4212-beautiful-november-wedding\/#review'>MTM Reviews<\/a><\/p>\n<p>Meet Lincoln & Team MTM: <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/vimeo.com\/51032621'>\"Meet Lincoln\" Video + see his Passion!!!<\/a>","Email":"momentsthatmatterphotography@gmail.com","IpAddress":"189.221.252.187","GroupId":49,"GroupName":"Insiders","JoinDate":1280185460,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-230711.png?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Moments That Matter","Id":230711,"Name":"Moments That Matter","IsOnline":false}}],"Id":"78709","Title":"Mexican Laws \/ Xrays \/ Documents \/ Help!","LastPostDate":1426726397},"Pages":{"TotalItems":13,"TotalPages":2,"CurrentPage":0,"NextPage":10,"PreviousPage":-1,"LastPage":10},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}